leo: Quick sync: we still get customers shipping undici into edge bundles. Need a single, copy-paste doc + tiny sample that shows the right pattern.

maya: Agreed. Short rule: never top-level import undici. Use globalThis.fetch when present, otherwise dynamic import undici at runtime.

oliver: Proposed tiny runtime helper (in thread):
```ts
// runtime/fetch-or-undici.ts
let cached: typeof fetch | undefined;
export async function runtimeFetch(): Promise<typeof fetch> {
  if (cached) return cached;
  if ((globalThis as any).fetch) return (cached = globalThis.fetch);
  try {
    const mod = await import('undici');
    return (cached = (mod as any).fetch);
  } catch (_) {
    try {
      // CJS fallback
      // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-var-requires
      const req = require('undici');
      return (cached = req.fetch);
    } catch (e) {
      throw new Error('No fetch available. Install undici or run on Node 18+.');
    }
  }
}
```

tara: Docs: show how to pass custom fetch into clientOptions and show tsconfig snippet: `{ "compilerOptions": { "lib": ["es2021","dom"] } }`. Call out @types/undici if they install it.

maya: Packaging note: keep conditional exports so CJS and ESM both work. Also mark undici as optionalDependency so installs are opt-in.

leo: Add a one-line troubleshooting FAQ: "fetch is not defined" -> either install undici or run on a runtime with fetch; ensure tsconfig includes dom for TS.

oliver: Runtime gotchas to mention: AbortSignal behavior differs across runtimes, streaming semantics vary. Recommend create a fresh AbortController per request; we could expose a small helper `newController()` in SDK utils.

ci-bot: CI #2601: packaging smoke passed on Node 18/20; edge bundle-size job confirms undici not present in edge-targeted build.

maya: Action items: (1) add runtime helper to SDK and use it internally, (2) update quickstart + three tiny sample apps (node-server, next-server, next-edge) showing optional `npm i undici`, (3) add TS troubleshooting blurb, (4) update CI matrix (Node 18/20, Next edge, Vercel, Cloudflare). I'll draft the PR.
